From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerome Tollet <jtollet@cisco.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [RFC] net/mlx5e: preserve XSK ownership on RX-ring-full redirect

When xsk_rcv_zc() cannot publish a descriptor because the userspace RX
ring is full, it recycles the XSK buffer before returning -ENOBUFS.  The
mlx5 legacy cyclic RQ releases its WQE later.  If the recycled buffer is
allocated again before that deferred release, freeing it a second time
creates an ABA ownership violation.

Mark this mlx5 XSK -ENOBUFS path as having transferred/recycled buffer
ownership so the deferred WQE release does not free it again.

This is a diagnostic RFC candidate, not an accepted upstream fix.  The
maintainers may prefer to make the generic XSK ownership contract more
explicit instead.

Signed-off-by: Jerome Tollet <jtollet@cisco.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xdp.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xdp.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xdp.c
index d8c7cb883..94568e9f6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xdp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xdp.c
@@ -334,8 +334,11 @@ bool mlx5e_xdp_handle(struct mlx5e_rq *rq,
 	case XDP_REDIRECT:
 		/* When XDP enabled then page-refcnt==1 here */
 		err = xdp_do_redirect(rq->netdev, xdp, prog);
-		if (unlikely(err))
+		if (unlikely(err)) {
+			if (rq->xsk_pool && err == -ENOBUFS)
+				__set_bit(MLX5E_RQ_FLAG_XDP_XMIT, rq->flags);
 			goto xdp_abort;
+		}
 		__set_bit(MLX5E_RQ_FLAG_XDP_XMIT, rq->flags);
 		__set_bit(MLX5E_RQ_FLAG_XDP_REDIRECT, rq->flags);
 		rq->stats->xdp_redirect++;
-- 
